# slug: ch27-coloring
# source: chapters/ch27.tex:97 (approximate line of \begin{algorithm})
# caption: Graph-coloring allocation with spill rewrite
# label: alg:ch27-coloring
# require: accurate interference graph, k interchangeable nonoverlapping registers, legal spill-rewrite policy
# ensure: assignment of ranges to registers or stack slots
# keywords: INPUT/OUTPUT/REQUIRE/ENSURE/FOR/FORALL/WHILE/IF/ELSE/RETURN

REQUIRE accurate interference graph, k interchangeable nonoverlapping registers, legal spill-rewrite policy
ENSURE assignment of ranges to registers or stack slots
build interference graph G with move edges marked
conservatively coalesce moves that keep G colorable
WHILE unprocessed nonprecolored nodes remain in G DO
  IF a nonprecolored node n with degree < k exists THEN
    push n on the stack and remove it from G
  ELSE
    choose a nonprecolored spill candidate n by cost over degree
    push n as a potential spill and remove it
  END IF
END WHILE
pop nodes, assign colors respecting fixed neighbors, mark true spills colorless
IF spills exist THEN
  insert spill code and rebuild affected regions
  repeat until no new spills
END IF

